prompt:
Use Three.js to implement a 3D lighting studio. Load lighting fixture models, allowing users to adjust light properties and positions and observe real-time shadow effects.

[Three.js Import Method (Must Be Followed Strictly)]
Use the following importmap in <head>, and import via ES Modules in <script type="module">:
<script type="importmap">
{ "imports": {
    "three": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/build/three.module.js",
    "three/addons/": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.170.0/examples/jsm/"
} }
</script>
<script type="module">
import * as THREE from 'three';
import { GLTFLoader } from 'three/addons/loaders/GLTFLoader.js';
import { OrbitControls } from 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js';
// Write your code here
</script>

[Model Loading]
(1) Use GLTFLoader to load assets/IridescenceLamp.glb and assets/Lantern.glb;
(2) Place the two lighting fixtures at (-2,0,0) and (2,0,0), respectively;

[Light System]
(3) Attach one PointLight inside each lighting fixture;
(4) Light intensity slider (id="intensitySlider", range 0-5, default 1);
(5) Light color picker (id="lightColor", type="color", default warm white #ffeedd);

[Scene Objects]
(6) Place a white sphere (radius=1) at the center as the illuminated object;
(7) Use a ground plane to receive shadows;

[Shadows]
(8) Enable renderer.shadowMap;
(9) Set castShadow = true for both PointLights;
(10) The sphere and lighting fixtures cast shadows, and the ground receives shadows;
(11) A "Shadow Toggle" button (id="shadowToggle") toggles the shadowMap on or off;

[OrbitControls]
(12) Support orbit viewing;

[HUD Display]
(13) HUD in the upper-left corner:
  - Number of lights (id="lightCount")
  - Shadow state (id="shadowState", on/off)
  - Current intensity (id="intensityValue")

[State Exposure (Required)]
Update window.__3D_STATE__ every frame:
  - modelLoaded: boolean (both models have finished loading)
  - lightCount: number
  - shadowEnabled: boolean
  - intensity: number
  - lightColor: string (hex)

Output a single standalone HTML file.
